'''Akaza''' (猗窩座, ''Akaza'') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in the [[Demon Slayer: Kimetsu no Yaiba Collaboration Event]]. He was added in [[Version 15.1 Update#Version 15.1.1 Update|Version 15.1.1]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Akaza
|image = E 763.png
|first appearance = [[Upper Rank Three - Akaza (Easy)]]
|money drop = 3,333¢ - 13,165¢
}}

==Enemy==
This decently fast Traitless midranger stands at a somewhat high range of 350 and pushes with closely-spaced Milti-Hits that reach up to 450 range with his [[Omni Strike|Omni Strikes]]. Most of his damage is concentrated in his third hit, which produces an [[Explosion]] that goes up to 575, chipping and eventually destroying whoever survives or evades his attacks. He's not too threatening on his own, however, as his attack cycle and foreswing are long enough for many melee attackers to sneak in hits and inflict heavy damage. He still shouldn't be underestimated when backed by other threats despite having a somewhat high knockback count and no immunities.

==Strategy==
Given his long attack frequency, it is recommended to use expendible attackers like [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] to sneak in good hits and quickly whittle him down. At higher magnifications, his third hit deals absurd damage that is guaranteed to instantly kill anything that doesn't outrange it, or the Explosion it creates (Additionally, units staggered by his first Multi-Hit are usually knocked into his third one); squishy backliners or midrangers like [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Awakened Ururun]] are ill-advised as a result. [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] is one of the best units to use against him, since he's able to snipe everything behind Akaza.

